{"item": "a1", "score": 2, "reason": "All four required decisions are correct and grounded in quotes: the immutable policy-eligible subset with static rejections kept separately, capacity computed at final serialized commit, no revision or routing change until preparation succeeds (the ACK is tied to the atomic change), and nonfatal per-route denials."}
{"item": "a2", "score": 1, "reason": "It makes no unsafe recommendation and grounds the optional second argument, unchanged credential-free DTOs, the signal not being a session or credential handle, and no browser/CLI split, but it omits R2 (cooperative cancellation with finite accounting still necessary), omits that AGP always supplies the options, and its migration and one-argument compatibility claims are unquoted."}
{"item": "a5", "score": 1, "reason": "The decisions are correct and mostly grounded, including AGP always supplying the options and no browser/CLI split, but its R2 claim that the work ledger provides lifetime safety when cancellation is ignored and its R4 no-reuse-after-commit claim are not supported by any quote; the adoption-outstanding note is a scope limit, not a hedge."}
{"item": "a3", "score": 1, "reason": "It correctly grounds deadline rechecking at application, no revision/RIB/ACK from an expired result, and reservation held until disposal with a single release, but it does not address R4 (a check only inside the final reducer is insufficient)."}
{"item": "a4", "score": 0, "reason": "It recommends applying the successful-attempt reset on OpenConfirm satisfaction, contradicting R1/R2's preserved retryAttempt = 4 and establishment-based success; this faithfully repeats a supplied instruction (document inadequacy, not reader invention), it only partially flags the resulting ambiguity, and it omits the exact-Established single reset (R3) and the distinction between scheduling cancellation and history reset (R4)."}
{"item": "a6", "score": 1, "reason": "The decisions are substantively correct with no unsafe recommendation, but decisive claims are unquoted: R1's projection details (retry-wait, identity reason, unchanged retryAttempt, no retryAt or active controller), and R3's level-recheck-not-permit behaviour and guard checks before a real acquisition."}
